A quick guide to building and installing tfkiss
------------------------------------------------

Requirements
------------

* CMake 3.16 or newer
* A C compiler with C17 support
* BlueZ development headers for the default Linux Bluetooth build

Configure and build out of tree:

    cmake -S . -B build
    cmake --build build
    ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure

The default installation prefix is `/usr/local`. Select another prefix while
configuring, for example:

    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/opt/tfkiss

Optional features are disabled unless stated otherwise:

    -DTFKISS_ENABLE_AXIP=ON       AXIP support
    -DTFKISS_ENABLE_XPID=ON       changeable PID support
    -DTFKISS_ENABLE_FLEXNET=ON    decoded FLEXNET node frames
    -DTFKISS_ENABLE_HIBAUD=ON     rates above 38400 baud (Linux only)
    -DTFKISS_ENABLE_BLUETOOTH=OFF disable Bluetooth (enabled by default on Linux)

Install after a successful build:

    sudo cmake --install build

The executable is installed in `sbin`; documentation and configuration are
installed below `share/tfkiss`. If `tfkiss.ini` already exists in the target
configuration directory, neither example configuration file is overwritten.
Review `tfkiss.ini` and `tfkiss.cfg` before starting tfkiss.

Packagers can stage an installation without root privileges:

    DESTDIR="$PWD/stage" cmake --install build
